[#:seon.task{:id "96ac997dcf2f"
             :name "hot-internals-pay-armed-validation"
             :kind :namespace
             :intent "Armed validation cost per call was Malli's regex driver for the :cat input plus -instrument-f's argument vector and always-on guard pair (~700-1300 B, 200-500 ns per armed call; ~6,600 armed calls per trivial agent form). Fixed in malli 43c6dca8 (pin c0c39ec5c), adopted at the next restart. Done when root re-runs tmp/contract-cost-opus/probe.clj on the new pin and the armed-validation share of a trivial eval (JFR, tmp/contract-cost-opus/agg.py) is measured; the remaining armed overhead is seon.instrument/arm-var!'s timing wrapper (~100 ns, 0 B) and the validators' own leaf work."
             :must-read #{seon.instrument/arm-var! seon.schema/canonical-reference-graph}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/perf-profile-2026-09-26.md" "docs/research/agent-platform/landing/contract-cost-opus-2026-09-26.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:id "7095e91b3f42"
             :name "an-oversized-refusal-hides-its-cause"
             :kind :function
             :intent "When an armed refusal's data exceeds the admission bound (a 7,872-byte :over-bound remainder), the wrapper answers only 'X :malli.core/invalid-input: the refusal could not be built.' (instrument.clj:633), with no path, expected schema or offending shape. That is how call-reach's set-for-sequential defect showed at HEAD. The refusal must name the member and path and let the floor bound the offending value."
             :must-read #{seon.instrument/compiled-wrapper}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/landing/task-log-2026-09-26.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:id "d7b76a5a0481"
             :name "explanation-schemas-have-no-producer"
             :kind :schema
             :intent "resources/seon/schemas/seon.instrument.explanation(s).edn and the :seon.instrument/explanations attribute have no producer since e604ee179; their generators (error.clj:2216-2427) and error_test.clj:1035-1107 only serve them. Retire them after an incremental schema-retraction proof on a branch."
             :must-read #{seon.error/instrumentation-prose}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/landing/error-text-2026-09-26.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:id "f985bfc97116"
             :name "instrumentation-is-jvm-global"
             :kind :namespace
             :intent "Instrumentation and Malli's function-schema registration are process-global (2,098 installed wrappers; instrument/apply! and malli.instrument change them for every test member), so the test runner must keep the ambient snapshot, drift and restore family and a member can damage shared Vars. Make wrappers and registrations per context so the C2 family (ambient-snapshot, restore-live-cluster-schema!, schema-restore-drift, run-vars!'s drift branch) can go in one cut."
             :must-read #{seon.instrument/apply! seon.test.runner/ambient-snapshot}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/landing/delete-r8-r6-r10-2026-09-26.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:id "a57e8b27de67"
             :name "contract-refusal-carries-wrapper-bookkeeping"
             :kind :function
             :intent "An agent's contract refusal reaches it with the wrapper's bookkeeping beside operation/expected/offending/problems: :seon.instrument/arglists, arity, arm, caller (\"sci.lang.Var (lang.cljc:217)\", the interpreter, never the author), check, fn (= operation), malli, problem-count, :seon.error/expected-shape and data-blob digests, :seon.error/doc, shown and result-id (~2.5 KB for one refused argument). Keep operation, expected, offending, problems (fix) and member; the rest is derivable from the operation's row or is evaluation evidence. The kernel side (err-minimal-opus) already drops the evaluator's frames and the duplicated link message."
             :must-read #{seon.instrument/compiled-wrapper seon.sci.kernel/failure-value}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/landing/err-minimal-opus-2026-09-26.md"}}]
